Response (FULL, NOT TRUNCATED):
Based on the details you provided, your Australian passport expires on December 1, 2028. Here is how you can verify that your document is fully valid for your visa application and upcoming travel:

1. **The Six-Month Validity Rule:** Most countries require your passport to be valid for at least six months beyond your planned date of entry or departure from their country. Because your passport expires in late 2028, you easily meet this time requirement for travel in the near future.
2. **Blank Pages:** Open your passport and check that you have enough blank visa pages. Many countries require at least one to two completely blank pages for entry stamps and the physical visa sticker.
